CRASH-03: reject a curve or time series without data instead of crashing

table_validate() reads the first entry and then loops over
table_getNextEntry(), which dereferences table->thisEntry. For an in-memory
table with no entries (a [CURVES] line with only the name and type, or a
time series whose only line has no value) table_getFirstEntry() returns FALSE
without setting thisEntry, which is still NULL, and the loop crashes. Return
an error for such a table. project_validate() reports it as ERROR 171 for a
curve and ERROR 173 for a time series, as it does for out-of-sequence data.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CRASH-03_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/table.c b/src/legacy/engine/table.c
index c7564d2..61614c3 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/table.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/table.c
@@ -311,6 +311,10 @@ int table_validate(TTable *table)
     if ( !result && table->file.mode == USE_FILE )
         return ERR_TABLE_FILE_READ;
 
+    // --- return error condition if table has no data at all
+    //     (project_validate reports ERROR 171 for a curve, 173 for a series)
+    if ( !result ) return ERR_TIMESERIES_SEQUENCE;
+
     // --- retrieve successive table entries and check for non-increasing x-values
     while ( table_getNextEntry(table, &x2, &y2) )
     {
